Threat Detection Engineering Example: cipher.exe Rule

Why?

cipher.exe is a built-in tool that can securely wipe free disk space. Its usage can indicate anti-forensics or attacker cleanup activities.

Detection is done by building a Custom wazuh rule (cipher_rule.xml):

This can be either done in the browser interface or in the CLI on Ubuntu.

For this lab, we'll do it through the Rules section under server management on the Wazuh web interface

<group name="windows,sysmon,cipher">
  <rule id="100005" level="13">
    <if_sid>61603</if_sid>
    <field name="win.eventdata.image" type="pcre2">cipher.exe</field>
    <match>cipher.exe</match>
    <description>Potential anti-forensics: cipher.exe is used to wipe data</description>
  </rule>
</group>



Restart Wazuh manager for the rule to apply.
